  "narrative": {
    "intro": "North Dakota has received $665M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 2,217 awards with an average award size of $300K. Obligations are down 19.0% year over year. Historical totals show multiyear variation: FY21 $780M, FY22 $973M, FY23 $803M, FY24 $980M, and FY25 $821M. The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buyer so far with $284M, followed by the Department of Defense with $169M and the Department of Transportation with $87.6M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC is the largest vendor with $263M, and WALSH FEDERAL LLC is second with $74.4M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations with $226M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction follows with $115M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial because they reflect fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have federal obligations in North Dakota changed recently?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 19.0% year over year. FY26 obligations are $665M compared with FY25 obligations of $821M. Historical year totals include FY24 $980M and FY22 $973M. The FY2026 total is a fiscal year to date figure and therefore partial."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in North Dakota?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services is the top buying agency with $284M, followed by the Department of Defense with $169M and the Department of Transportation with $87.6M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC is the top vendor with $263M, followed by WALSH FEDERAL LLC with $74.4M and PACKET DIGITAL LLC with $36.8M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations with $226M, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction has $115M."
      }
    ]
  },
